add('executor','C3RehearseAdmit',f"""Rehearse the C3 landing in a scratch clone so the L1 integrates a known-good set. In {S('C3RehearseAdmit')} clone the lane (`git clone -q --no-local {L}`; scratch-local git identity via `git -C ... config`). Take the staged entries {SH}/knowledge/corpus/knowledge/duplicate-verdict-identity.md and duplicate-verdict-taxonomy-r24.md; produce the two lane entries `corpus/knowledge/duplicate-verdict-identity.md` and `corpus/knowledge/duplicate-verdict-byte-equality.md` with: provenance trio first (`source:` lines citing the lane ids S216 statx, S217 Broder, S218 link, S219 cmp with URL and anchor; `verified-at: 2026-10-25`; `recheck: 365d` plus the command that re-verifies), `ground: F3 — duplicate verdicts`, claim text rewritten in your own words (remove the staged text's `CANNOT-ANSWER.md` pointer, which does not exist in this lane), a `## What this does NOT establish` section, a `## Gate` section with https URLs, `opened: 2026-10-25`, `snapshot:` paths under census/round-29/sources/, located quotes (<=25 words, locator token), one `- ADMIT:` and one `- REJECT:` line with reasons. Use the pinned snapshots under {W}/sources/ if a sibling has already delivered them, otherwise download your own into the scratch census/round-29/sources/. Add the four rows to scratch corpus/SOURCES.md (normalize as the C3MirrorValidate item describes), add the F3 coverage-map row text to scratch corpus/README.md (see the existing F3 row at {L}/corpus/README.md line 41: add both new entries as backticked `knowledge/<name>` paths in the entries column, keep ground cell beginning F3), then run in the scratch clone: the C3 counters of the preregistration (grounded F3 count, row count, `tools/souji-coverage-agreement.py` at the scratch commit, `tools/souji-gate-check.py`, `sources-census.sh validate --file`, the C1 counter with `--list-rev`). Deliver the two entry files ({D('duplicate-verdict-identity.md')}, {D('duplicate-verdict-byte-equality.md')}), the README row text ({D('readme-f3-row.md')}) and the counter outputs in your report. Expected: F3 count 2, rows 143, coverage `grounded=15 mapped=15 dangling=0 mismatches=0`, gate `entries=2 ok=2 ... fail=0`, census rc 0, C1 k1=0.""")
add('executor','PreReportGateReadiness',f"""Produce the round-end landing checklist, executed. Read {L}/tools/souji-pre-report-gate.sh, {L}/tests/fixtures/r27-pre-report-gate.sh, {L}/tools/souji-landing-gate.py (CLI section) and the prompt's commit/landing rules ({L}/.ufo/prompts/souji-round-29.md section 6 item 4). In a scratch clone ({S('PreReportGateReadiness')}) run the pre-report gate at base and describe exactly what inputs it needs (report path, lane hash, ls-remote output form, SHONEN count) and what each exit code means. Deliver {D('landing-checklist.md')}: an ordered, copy-pasteable list of the commands the L1 must run at round end (full-40 tip from `jj-lane.sh state`, ls-remote check, `grep -c '^## SHONEN'`, census exit 0, misroot sweep `git -C /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin status --porcelain`, landing gate rc expectations given `.ufo/waves/` is gitignored — the r28 closure routed that the gate's report check can never evaluate committed reports: say what rc 2 `COULD-NOT-EVALUATE` means and how to tell it from a finding), each with expected output shape verified by you at base.""")
add('executor','QCriteriaRedBefore',f"""Prove that three proposed QUALITY criteria can fail. The L1 proposes: Q60 a frozen counter's exclusion clause is applied as written and the lane records its reading in the same lesson before any after-data (r28 C2: the frozen text excluded the S215 row; the lane self-ruled a miss at 139 while the closure applied the exclusion and verified 138); Q61 a receipt/manifest counter must read committed bytes at the landed revision (git ls-tree/cat-file), never the lane's disk, and a capture must account every ignored path (r28 C3: 152 manifest records absent from git); Q62 a used-by/source citation is bidirectional: row used-by names the entry and the entry's source: line names the row (r28 defect 5: S215). For each, write a concrete checker command (one line, git plumbing or the committed tools) that returns non-clean at base {BASE} for the named reason and clean on a minimal scratch repair, running both in scratch ({S('QCriteriaRedBefore')}, clone of the lane). Q62's checker is `python3 -B {C1T}`; Q61's is `python3 -B {C2C}`; for Q60 design the checker (e.g. a scan that a lesson's Gate/Findings carries a `reading:` line for every frozen exclusion clause, tested against {L}/corpus/lessons/round-28.md which lacks it). Deliver {D('q60-q62-red-before.tsv')} (criterion, checker command, base result, repaired result, delta) with verbatim outputs.""")
add('executor','StaleStatementSweep',f"""Sweep the lane's own records for self-assessment statements that disagree with observed state beyond the four frozen stale statements ({STALE}). Targets: (1) every remaining statement in {L}/LOG.md, {L}/SCORECARD.md, {L}/corpus/lessons/round-2[5-8].md, {L}/corpus/README.md, {L}/SHONEN.md describing the r26/r27/r28 wave-evidence manifests, receipts or `sha256sum -c` outcomes (grep for manifest, sha256sum, newline, improperly, malformed, 152, 1382); (2) SHONEN.md and the SCORECARD axes/capabilities tables: for each backticked path or command, run the cheap existence/exit check at the lane tip (read-only) and list those that do not resolve. Deliver {D('stale-sweep.tsv')} (file, line, statement, observed, verdict agree/disagree/unverifiable, command) — the disagreeing rows are candidates for a later round and are NOT added to the frozen C1 list. Paste the sweep commands so the negative claim carries its sweep.""")
add('executor','SeatResultsTool',f"""Write a small stdlib python3 script that summarizes a wave `<wave>-results.json` for the round report. Deliver {D('results-summary.py')}. Study the shape of {L}/census/round-28/waves/w1-results.json (per seat: name, agent, id, status, final output) and {L}/census/round-28/waves/summary.tsv; the script takes `--results PATH` (and optionally `--spec PATH` to map item ids to roles when the agent field is missing) and prints: seat count, role mix (agent field), status histogram, the list of seats whose status is not completed with the first 200 characters of their last error/output (dead or aborted seats), and seats whose final output starts with `[WAIT]` or lacks a report file under a `--report-dir` (check `<report-dir>/<name>.md` existence). Output is stable, tab-separated sections, exit 0 always except unreadable input (exit 2). Test it on the r28 results file and paste the output; confirm its totals against `python3 -c` one-liners you write independently (64 seats expected; role mix executor 20, reviewer 12, scribe 8, critic 6, mutation-tester 6, scout 6, connector 2, sentinel 2, simplifier 2).""")
add('executor','SourcesDiffTool',f"""Write a small stdlib python3 script that diffs the SOURCES.md registry between two committed revisions for the round report's Sources & frontier section. Deliver {D('sources-diff.py')}. Usage `--root LANE --from REV --to REV` (full 40-hex revisions, read through `git show`): print rows before->after (count by the CORPUS.md census regex, 0-3 leading spaces), tier histogram and status histogram before and after, the ids added with tier/status/kind, and for ids present in both revisions every in-place cell change as `old -> new` per column (only status, recheck and used-by may legitimately change; flag any other column change as `APPEND-ONLY-VIOLATION`). Test on {L} at `3a2a80d0d18940a5e352ebc526da22a57dad83c4` -> `fec846dd1781a414ae3a7d71d2d8fa2fb17900eb` (r28: rows 135 -> 139, S212-S215 added) and paste the output; cross-check the counts against the CORPUS.md census one-liners. Also show it flags a synthetic violation in a scratch clone (scratch per contract: change a `tier` cell in a commit there).""")
