add('scribe','C1Corrections',f"""Draft the append-only correction blocks for the four frozen stale statements ({STALE}): LOG.md:1758, SCORECARD.md:23, corpus/lessons/round-28.md:22 and :40. Open each line first. The facts, which you must re-derive yourself from committed bytes before writing them (`git -C {L} archive {BASE} census/round-26/waves | tar -x -C <scratch>` then python3 hashlib over the manifest; or `python3 -B {C2C} --root {L} --rev {BASE}`): the r26 manifest holds 1382 records, 152 of them name files absent from the committed tree (they were ignored by nested .gitignore files copied into the capture and by root patterns), 14 committed paths have no record, and the two backslash-escaped lines are valid GNU escapes that this host's uutils sha256sum 0.8.0 cannot parse. Deliver {D('c1-corrections.md')} containing three fenced blocks to append at the tail of each file (LOG.md, SCORECARD.md, corpus/lessons/round-28.md), each block starting its lines with `R29-CORRECTION <file>:<line>` exactly (the lesson block names both `corpus/lessons/round-28.md:22` and `corpus/lessons/round-28.md:40` in one line), stating the observed numbers with their command, saying the original sentence is superseded not edited, and saying what is still true. No new claims beyond the evidence you re-derived. State the revision your numbers are measured at.""")
add('scribe','EntryIdentity',f"""Draft the knowledge entry corpus/knowledge/duplicate-verdict-identity.md as a deliverable ({D('entry-identity.md')}). Open the three sources YOURSELF this run and quote from the bytes you opened: https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/statx.2.html, https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/link.2.html, and the Broder paper at https://www.cs.princeton.edu/courses/archive/spring13/cos598C/broder97resemblance.pdf (the DOI https://doi.org/10.1109/SEQUEN.1997.666900 returns 202/0 bytes). The staged package version is at {SH}/knowledge/corpus/knowledge/duplicate-verdict-identity.md — treat it as a lead, not evidence; re-ground every claim. Shape: front matter `source:` lines citing lane ids S216 (statx), S217 (Broder), S218 (link) with URL, section anchor and edition; `verified-at: 2026-10-25`; `recheck: 365d` plus the exact re-verify command; `ground: F3 — duplicate verdicts`; then Claim (path multiplicity is not file multiplicity; identity fields stx_ino/stx_nlink/stx_btime/stx_mnt_id; resemblance and containment named as vocabulary only), `## What this does NOT establish` (btime filesystem-dependent, mnt id kernel 6.8 uniqueness, Broder is document similarity not byte equality, no receipt class chosen), `## Lane link` (existing entry {L}/corpus/knowledge/dupe-finders-detect-then-act.md already requires distinct `stat -c '%d:%i'`; PROVINCE F3; the `duplicate` receipt class remains an OPERATOR decision), and `## Gate` with https URLs, `opened: 2026-10-25`, `snapshot:` paths under census/round-29/sources/ (statx.2.html, link.2.html, broder97resemblance.txt), located quotes of at most 25 words each with a locator, one `- ADMIT:` line and one `- REJECT:` line with reasons (reject the staged claim wording you refuse, e.g. the reference to a nonexistent CANNOT-ANSWER.md, or a Broder clustering sentence you could not locate). No `|` characters in quotes.""")
add('scribe','EntryByteEquality',f"""Draft knowledge entry corpus/knowledge/duplicate-verdict-byte-equality.md as a deliverable ({D('entry-byte-equality.md')}). Open the sources YOURSELF this run: https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man1/cmp.1.html, https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/link.2.html and the Broder PDF https://www.cs.princeton.edu/courses/archive/spring13/cos598C/broder97resemblance.pdf. The staged version is {SH}/knowledge/corpus/knowledge/duplicate-verdict-taxonomy-r24.md — a lead only; re-ground it. Lane ids: S219 (cmp), S217 (Broder), S218 (link). Claim: `cmp` is a documented byte-by-byte oracle with a three-valued exit status (0 same, 1 different, 2 trouble), so a verdict that maps 2 to different misclassifies an unreadable file; the existing lane rule requiring `cmp` byte equality ({L}/SKILL.md receipt/duplicate guard text, {L}/corpus/knowledge/dupe-finders-detect-then-act.md) is thereby grounded in a primary source; resemblance and containment remain vocabulary for a later near-duplicate class; the threshold is an operator decision and this entry proposes none. Include provenance trio and `ground: F3 — duplicate verdicts`, `## What this does NOT establish`, `## Lane link`, `## Gate` (https URLs, opened 2026-10-25, snapshot paths under census/round-29/sources/, located quotes <=25 words with locator tokens, one ADMIT and one REJECT line with reasons). Check how the cmp(1) page renders the exit-status sentence in raw HTML before quoting (markup between words breaks whitespace-collapsed matching) and quote what the bytes show.""")
add('scribe','SourcesRows',f"""Draft the four new SOURCES.md rows for the lane registry, S216 statx(2), S217 Broder 1997 (author-hosted PDF URL; DOI noted in the anchor cell without a pipe), S218 link(2), S219 cmp(1), as a deliverable ({D('sources-rows.md')}) in the exact 11-column schema of {L}/corpus/SOURCES.md (read its header and three recent rows first; NF=13 when split on the pipe character; no pipe inside any cell). Open each source yourself this run to ground `anchor` (section + edition: man-pages release line and date as the page shows it; diffutils version line for cmp; paper title/venue/year), `teaches` (one grounded learner benefit, not a restatement of the staged text), `scope`, `tier` (man pages tier A for their scope; Broder tier B for vocabulary of similarity, not for filesystem equality), `kind`, `status` mined, `opened` 2026-10-25, `recheck` ISO date or cadence, `used-by` per this assignment: S216 -> corpus/knowledge/duplicate-verdict-identity.md; S217 -> both entries; S218 -> both entries; S219 -> corpus/knowledge/duplicate-verdict-byte-equality.md. Also draft the Search log note (rule 5: question, where searched, date, identified/screened/included/excluded counts from the F3 merge-package scan, reasons, stop rationale) and a Paths line. Compare to the staged rows at {SH}/SOURCES.append.md (campaign ids S117 S118 S122 S136) and list every cell you changed and why.""")
add('scribe','LessonGateF3',f"""Draft the `## Gate` block for corpus/lessons/round-29.md ({D('lesson-gate.md')}). It must record, as a table like {L}/corpus/lessons/round-28.md `## Gate`: for each new row S216-S219 the URL, access date 2026-10-25 and a located quote of at most 25 words (open the sources yourself and quote bytes you opened); ADMIT decisions for the two entries; REJECT decisions with reason and flip condition for at least these staged F3-adjacent entries from {SH}/knowledge/corpus/knowledge/: near-duplicate-threshold-r28.md, near-duplicate-operating-point-r28.md, near-duplicate-relations-r29.md, near-duplicate-literature-identity-r33.md, near-duplicate-threshold-source-r34.md (document-similarity ground outside PROVINCE F3's byte-identical scope — open each and confirm or refute from its text), duplicate-receipt-class-decision-r25.md and -r26.md (operator-decision records, not facts); the normalization notes (recheck prose stripped, anchor rewritten), the collision-guard result placeholder `<collisions=N>` and the quarantine verdict for campaign register row S118 `<verdict>` (the L1 fills placeholders from other seats; keep them visibly marked, invent no numbers); the SOURCES touched-row log (old->new for status/recheck/used-by changes, to be filled from the C1 repair table); and an explicit note that a spot-check by a non-author is pending (the lane's own seats do not count). Also draft `## Findings`, `## Receipts`, `## Residuals` headings with the evidence pointers named in the preregistration {PR}.""")
add('scribe','ReadmeProvinceF3',f"""Draft three documentation edits as deliverables ({D('docs-f3.md')}): (1) the replacement text for the F3 line of the corpus/README.md coverage map ({L}/corpus/README.md line 41) listing the held entry `knowledge/dupe-finders-detect-then-act.md` plus the two new backticked entries `knowledge/duplicate-verdict-identity.md` and `knowledge/duplicate-verdict-byte-equality.md`, keeping the ground cell beginning `F3` and status wording honest (frontier, entries held; F3 stays frontier, the `duplicate` receipt class remains an operator decision) — check {L}/tools/souji-coverage-agreement.py to ensure the entries column format satisfies it; plus the new `### Frontier (r29)` and Corrections-style lines for corpus/README.md that follow the file's append-only habit (read its r24-r28 sections and imitate; never rewrite older lines); (2) a `## Round 29 boundary note` for PROVINCE.md in the style of the Round 13-21 notes (what F3 now holds, what it does not: no receipt class, no near-duplicate threshold, no tool change; Core/Frontier unchanged); (3) the SKILL.md rule text for F3 (one decision-table row in the style of the existing rows, read {L}/SKILL.md lines 1-120 and 167-226 first): a duplicate verdict compares inodes (stat %d:%i or statx), treats `cmp` exit 2 as trouble not different, and does not exist as a receipt class. Every sentence you add must be supportable by a file or command you can name.""")
