add('scribe','ScorecardLogSkeleton',f"""Draft skeletons ({D('scorecard-log-skeleton.md')}) the L1 will fill after data: (1) a `### Round 29 measurements` table for {L}/SCORECARD.md in the exact column layout of the Round 28 table (read SCORECARD.md lines 17-25) with rows C1/C2/C3, before values taken from the frozen files (`census/round-29/records/controls.tsv`: C1 `mismatches=10`, C2 `failed=152 uncovered=14`, C3 `F3 entries 0, rows 139`), after cells as `<AFTER>` and measured commit cells as `<MEASURED>` placeholders — never fill an after value; (2) the capabilities-table rows (columns `name | what it can now do | evidence pointer | first-working round`) for the two instruments only if their demonstrations run (mark `<enters only if the demonstration passes>`): declared-record agreement audit (C1 tool) and committed-bytes wave-evidence capture (C2); (3) a LOG.md entry in the style of the Round 28 entry at the tail of {L}/LOG.md (read it), headed `## 2026-10-25 — Round 29 attempt 1: ...` with placeholder lines; (4) the Planned bullet for r30 text taking in the r28 routed defect 3 (landing-gate cannot evaluate committed reports because `.ufo/waves/` is gitignored) and the stale-sweep remainder. Placeholders are bracketed `<...>`; no number you cannot cite to a file.""")
add('scribe','ReportSkeleton',f"""Draft the round-report skeleton ({D('report-skeleton.md')}) for /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/.ufo/reports/round-29/souji.md. Read the required sections and marker rule in {L}/.ufo/prompts/../../../.ufo/prompts/souji-round-29.md (path: /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/.ufo/prompts/souji-round-29.md section 4), {L}/SHONEN.md (four boxes), and an earlier report /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/.ufo/reports/round-28/souji.md for house style. Sections in order: Work performed (opens by naming claims C1 calibration, C2 operability, C3 coverage), Landed changes, Before -> after measurements (one per claim with counting command and measured commit), Sources & frontier (rows before->after with counting command, rows added by tier, rows touched old->new, frontier advanced, `Assimilation:` line naming theme F3 from merge/souji and `considerthese/` absent), Trend verdicts (expansion, quality, discernment), SHONEN (exactly one `## SHONEN` heading and one `[~]` or `[ ]` line per SHONEN.md box; `[x]` only with a named non-author verifier), plus the extras: round shape, wave sizes and role mix, dead seats, Stale-lane line, tool installs, misroot sweep result, inherited-state naming, and the routed-defect disposition table for the six r28 closure defects. Placeholders only (`<...>`) for values not yet measured.""")
