add('scout','OpenLink',f"""Open https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/link.2.html yourself. Deliver: the page version/date line; located quotes (<=25 words) for 'creates a new link (also known as a hard link) to an existing file', 'impossible to tell which name was the original' and any cross-device or EXDEV statement and `link()` on directories/symlinks behaviour the page states; check the quotes in the staged entries at {SH}/knowledge/corpus/knowledge/duplicate-verdict-identity.md and duplicate-verdict-taxonomy-r24.md for verbatim accuracy (quote marks, apostrophes, `original` quoting) and report mismatches. Also open https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/stat.2.html (st_dev, st_ino) and say whether that is a better anchor for the (device, inode) pair rule `stat -c '%d:%i'` the lane's existing entry requires (quote it).""")
add('scout','OpenCmp',f"""Open https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man1/cmp.1.html yourself and report how it renders `Exit status is 0 if inputs are the same, 1 if different, 2 if trouble` (raw HTML bytes via `curl -sSL` and rendered text): markup between words, exact punctuation, the page's version/date line (diffutils version) and the DESCRIPTION line 'Compare two files byte by byte'. Check also whether `-s`/`--silent` and `-l` change the exit contract, and whether `cmp` behaves for the same file given twice or for hard links (what the page says). Compare against the staged entry {SH}/knowledge/corpus/knowledge/duplicate-verdict-taxonomy-r24.md and list claim -> supported? Quote <=25 words per item with the section locator.""")
add('scout','OpenBroder',f"""Open the Broder paper at https://www.cs.princeton.edu/courses/archive/spring13/cos598C/broder97resemblance.pdf (download into /var/tmp/souji-r29-OpenBroder/, `pdftotext`) and the DOI https://doi.org/10.1109/SEQUEN.1997.666900 (record what curl returns: expect 202 and 0 bytes) and Crossref https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1109/SEQUEN.1997.666900 (record title, container, year, DOI). Establish whether the Princeton PDF is the SEQUENCES 1997 paper (title, authors, abstract, page header lines) and say how you know. Deliver located quotes (<=25 words) for: resemblance r(A, B) and containment c(A, B) definitions; 'roughly the same'; the section number/title that defines them (the staged row cites section 2 'Definitions as set intersection problems' — confirm or correct the exact heading); the 50% clustering example sentence the staged entry paraphrases ('containing only identical documents', 'a mixture of exact duplicates and similar') — locate it or report it absent. Note the paper is about web documents, not byte-identical files.""")
add('scout','F3RejectCandidates',f"""Judge the staged F3-adjacent entries for scope. Read PROVINCE.md ({L}/PROVINCE.md, F3 line and Refuses), {L}/corpus/QUALITY.md (admission bar, Q1-Q15 + the later rows that govern entries) and each staged entry in {SH}/knowledge/corpus/knowledge/ whose name matches `near-duplicate-*` or `duplicate-*` (list them with `ls`). For each: its ground, whether its sources are about byte-identical files or document similarity, whether its claims are facts or operator-decision records, whether it cites a source the lane could re-open, and your verdict ADMIT/REJECT with reason and flip condition. The admit set is already planned as `duplicate-verdict-identity.md` and the taxonomy entry renamed `duplicate-verdict-byte-equality.md`; say whether you agree each belongs and whether any other staged entry beats them. Deliver {D('f3-scope-table.tsv')} (entry, ground, byte-identical-or-similarity, fact-or-decision, verdict, reason, flip).""")
add('scout','SiblingOverlapScan',f"""Sibling-overlap scan for the F3 theme (duplicate / identity / byte-equality verdicts). Read-only. In /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin run grep over `*/PROVINCE.md`, `*/SKILL.md`, `*/corpus/README.md` and `*/corpus/knowledge/*.md` for `duplicate`, `byte-identical`, `hard link`, `inode`, `cmp(1)`, `statx`, `Broder`, `resemblance`, `near-duplicate`, `dedup` (skip {L}); tabulate by lane and file with the exact command. Judge whether any sibling claims this ground (chousa owns research method; kasegi/mori/tsukuroi/kama may touch dedup or host files). Report adjacency: ground another lane holds is reported not absorbed. Also check whether the fleet root AXES/MISSION/CORPUS texts mention duplicate-verdict ownership. Deliver {D('sibling-overlap.tsv')} and a verdict `no sibling claims F3` or the contested rows.""")
add('scout','SliceRecheck',f"""Hand-check the souji quarantine-slice rows that point at the web (read-only; the register is {'/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokuknow/.ufo/waves/corpus-expansion-1/absent-defect-register.md'} — never edit, never run campaign tools). Derive the souji slice with the awk in {L}/.ufo/prompts/souji-round-29.md section 6 item 10 into /var/tmp/souji-r29-SliceRecheck/, then for campaign rows S114 (git-scm.com/docs/git-prune), S126 (docs.gtk.org/gio/method.File.trash.html) and S138 (the Qiita page) re-open the cited URL today and locate the register's quote (or its truncated form) with a located quote of at most 25 words; report present/absent and any markup difference. Compare with {L}/census/round-24/records/slice-verdicts.tsv and {L}/census/round-27 re-open notes (grep the lessons for `slice`). Report the verdict per row in the gate vocabulary accepted/unverifiable/refused with reason. These rows are NOT appended this round; the check is quality re-verification.""")
# ---------------- REVIEWERS (8)
add('reviewer','ReDeriveC1',f"""Independently re-derive the C1 base counter WITHOUT the tool. Using only `git -C {L}` plumbing (`show`, `ls-tree`, `cat-file`) at {BASE}, plain awk/grep/python written by you, compute: (a) K1 forward — each SOURCES.md row's used-by paths that do not exist or do not contain the row id; (b) K1 reverse — knowledge entries whose front-matter source: lines cite an S-id whose row does not list the entry; (c) K2 — for each line of {STALE} whether the phrase sits at file:line and whether a line starting `R29-CORRECTION ` follows. Compare with the tool's output (`python3 -B {C1T} --root {L} --rev {BASE} --list-rev {PRE}`: k1=6 k2=4). Report agreement or every discrepancy (e.g. a front-matter detection difference: what counts as the end of front matter, entries whose source lines use a different shape, rows using `;` separators). Also say whether the counter could produce a false zero on any registry shape you can construct.""")
add('reviewer','ReDeriveC2',f"""Independently re-derive the C2 base counter WITHOUT {C2C}. Export {BASE} committed bytes (`git -C {L} archive {BASE} census/round-26/waves census/round-27/waves census/round-28/waves | tar -x -C /var/tmp/souji-r29-ReDeriveC2/`) and write your own verifier in python3 (handle GNU backslash-escaped records, count failed = record whose file is absent or hash differs, uncovered = file/symlink in the dir with no record). Compare per round with the frozen counter's `r26 records=1382 failed=152 uncovered=14`, r27 and r28. Report any discrepancy and its cause (e.g. symlinks, `.gitkeep`, the manifest counted as uncovered, `summary.tsv`). Also test the frozen counter on a directory name containing a space or non-UTF-8 bytes in a scratch git repo (init with -C) and report whether it crashes (rc must be 1 or 2, never a traceback); report tracebacks as findings.""")
add('reviewer','VerifySourcesQuotes',f"""Independently verify the located quotes planned for the C3 entries against live pages. Open https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/statx.2.html, https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/link.2.html and https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man1/cmp.1.html now and confirm, with byte-level evidence (curl -sSL then grep on the RAW HTML as the lane gate matches whitespace-collapsed raw bytes; see {L}/tools/souji-gate-check.py QUOTE matching), each of: statx `stx_ino`, `stx_nlink`, `stx_btime`, `stx_mnt_id` struct lines; link(2) 'creates a new link (also known as a hard link) to an existing file' and 'impossible to tell which name was the'; cmp(1) the exit-status sentence. For each quote that the raw bytes do not carry verbatim (markup `<b>`, `&amp;`, HTML entities for quotes/apostrophes), report the byte-exact form the lane gate would need. Verdict per quote: gate-matchable-verbatim yes/no, with the fix.""")
add('reviewer','VerifyBroder',f"""Independently verify the Broder source choice. Fetch https://www.cs.princeton.edu/courses/archive/spring13/cos598C/broder97resemblance.pdf and run `pdftotext`; locate the exact lines for resemblance, containment, 'roughly the same'. Check provenance: does the PDF's text (title, authors Andrei Z. Broder, abstract, page headers) match the SEQUENCES 1997 paper registered at DOI 10.1109/SEQUEN.1997.666900 (fetch https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1109/SEQUEN.1997.666900 for title/authors/container)? Assess honestly whether an author-hosted course-archive copy is an acceptable row `source` for a tier-B row whose scope is `vocabulary of document-similarity verdicts` (CORPUS.md SOURCES contract: anchor = section/page plus revision; tier B = strong secondary) and whether the row should name the DOI as canonical in the anchor cell. Check the claim that the DOI landing page returns 202/0 bytes (`curl -sSIL`). Verdict: row admissible yes/no and under what wording; list wording defects in the staged row at {SH}/SOURCES.append.md (grep `^| S118 `).""")
add('reviewer','AuditPreregQ',f"""Audit the frozen preregistration {PR} against the lane's QUALITY rows Q55-Q59 ({L}/corpus/QUALITY.md) and the prompt's claim-sizing rules ({L}/.ufo/prompts/souji-round-29.md section 6 item 9 is not present in the file at that number — read /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/.ufo/prompts/souji-round-29.md lines 417-439 'Claim sizing'). Check: each after-state is one concrete value re-derivable with one command over committed bytes; no universal clause without enumeration; calibration claim counts mismatches between self-assessment and observed state (is C1 such a claim, given K1 concerns SOURCES registry rather than SCORECARD/SHONEN — judge honestly and propose the strictest additional observable that would bind SCORECARD/SHONEN claims without changing frozen targets, as an attack not an amendment); a do-nothing control cannot reach each target; the target literals quote the counters' own output shapes (Q58); distinct axes (Q59: run `python3 -B {L}/tools/souji-axis-check.py --prereg {PR} --scorecard {L}/SCORECARD.md`); causal separability. Deliver numbered findings with the exact sentence in the prereg and what is wrong or fine.""")
add('reviewer','ReviewControls',f"""Review the L1's controls ({L}/census/round-29/controls.sh and its output {L}/census/round-29/records/controls.tsv). For each of C1, C2, C3: is the do-nothing control and each junk control the CHEAPEST state that skips the claimed work? Propose and RUN (in your own scratch clone, per contract) cheaper or sneakier junk states and score them with the frozen counters ({C1T}, {C2C}, and the C3 counters named in {PR}): e.g. C1 — delete the registry rows that mismatch (does that count?), rename entries; C2 — replace blobs so hashes match, add symlinks.tsv listing every path as a symlink with matching target text for non-symlinks, make manifest.sha256 itself include records for files that exist; C3 — an entry with `ground: F3` citing four brand-new junk rows with used-by set and snapshots of empty files and a gate quote that matches the empty snapshot. Report which sneaky states reach the target counters; every one that does is a gameability finding with the strictest fix (stricter-only).""")
add('reviewer','DefectDisposition',f"""Produce the disposition table for the six routed defects of {L}/corpus/lessons/round-28-verifier-spotcheck.md (section Routed defects). Read the section, then {PR} and the wave items in {W}/../make-spec.py (the generator of this wave; read-only). For each defect 1-6 state: which claim/item addresses it, what observable shows it closed (command), or why it is not addressed this round (defect 3: the landing gate cannot evaluate committed reports because `.ufo/waves/` is now gitignored — not claimed; say what minimal honest handling the report needs, and whether the C2 capture directory `census/round-N/waves/` could be pointed at by the gate next round: read {L}/tools/souji-landing-gate.py report-discovery code and cite lines). Also check `{L}/corpus/lessons/` for any `operator-*.md` teaching not yet reflected in QUALITY.md/SKILL.md (list the files; sweep command). Deliver {D('defect-disposition.tsv')}.""")
add('reviewer','CalibrationLedger',f"""Calibrate the lane's self-assessment against observed state (read-only). Read {L}/SCORECARD.md axes table (lines 9-15), the Saturation line, {L}/SHONEN.md and {L}/corpus/README.md coverage map. Re-derive with commands the observable facts they assert: the number of SOURCES rows and the tier/status histograms (use the census commands from /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/CORPUS.md 'Census' block at {BASE}), the number of knowledge entries and which ground: F<k> headers exist (`grep -lE '^ground: F' ...`), the capabilities table row count, whether each SHONEN [~] pointer resolves. Report every place where a self-assessed number, count, verdict or pointer disagrees with the re-derived value, with file:line, the self-assessed text, the observed value and the command. This is the evidence base for the calibration axis; do not edit anything.""")
# ---------------- CRITICS (8)
add('critic','AttackC1',f"""Attack claim C1 ({PR}). Is `mismatches=0` a vacuous or gameable target? Construct concrete cheating states (scratch repos per contract) that reach k1=0 k2=0 with the frozen tool {C1T} while the self-assessment is still wrong: e.g. a correction marker line that states nothing true, a marker copied verbatim into the file tail, used-by cells pointing at lesson files that merely mention the id, removing source: lines from entries, a registry row demoted to rejected. For each, say whether the tool accepts it and what strictly stronger check (stricter-only) would reject it. Judge whether the claim measures calibration (self-assessment vs observed state) or only bookkeeping consistency, and say honestly whether the r28 routed defect 2 is closed by K2 or only relabelled. Deliver numbered attacks with scratch evidence.""")
add('critic','AttackC2',f"""Attack claim C2 ({PR}). The frozen counter {C2C} trusts `symlinks.tsv` and a manifest the same tool wrote. Construct cheating states in scratch (per contract) that reach failed=0 uncovered=0 floor_violations=0 while evidence is actually lost or untrue: a capture that silently drops files into excluded.tsv (not read by the counter), a symlinks.tsv that lists a regular-file path (does the counter require mode 120000?), a manifest listing hashes of empty files for tracked files with identical blobs, duplicated records, a record path with `..`, a second manifest name, a waves dir whose manifest is a symlink. Also: does failed=0 prove the receipt equals the SOURCE evidence (the counter never compares to .ufo/waves)? Propose stricter-only additions (e.g. require excluded.tsv rows to carry the source sha256 and a count line in summary). Deliver numbered attacks with evidence.""")
add('critic','AttackC3',f"""Attack claim C3 ({PR}). Targets: F3-grounded entries 0->2 by `grep -lE '^ground: F3'`; rows 139->143; coverage-agreement; gate-check; census. Is expansion credit real? Judge honestly: (i) do the two entries add coverage-map ground the lane did not hold (compare {L}/corpus/knowledge/dupe-finders-detect-then-act.md, which already requires distinct `stat -c '%d:%i'` and `cmp`; read it fully) or restate it with citations (a quality/depth move, not coverage)? (ii) is the Broder paper (document similarity) inside PROVINCE F3's scope (byte-identical copies) — PROVINCE.md; the r28 gate rejected staged S216 near-duplicate paper as F3 ground and said reconsider when the duplicate-class decision opens; (iii) can a junk pair reach the targets (see {L}/census/round-29/records/controls.tsv). Say what would make the claim a restatement and propose the stricter-only observable (e.g. each entry adds >=1 statement absent from the existing entry, checked by a command). Deliver numbered findings.""")
add('critic','ScopeCriticF3',f"""Scope critic for the two planned entries. Read {SH}/knowledge/corpus/knowledge/duplicate-verdict-identity.md and duplicate-verdict-taxonomy-r24.md, {L}/PROVINCE.md (Owns, Refuses, F3), {L}/SKILL.md (receipt taxonomy and the duplicate-config guard text), {L}/corpus/QUALITY.md (Q1-Q15 and the entry rules). For each paragraph of each staged entry decide: in scope (byte-identical copies, inode identity, the cmp oracle), borderline (document-similarity vocabulary, statx btime/mnt_id origin fields — F4 ground?), or out (operator decisions, nonexistent files such as CANNOT-ANSWER.md). Produce a keep/cut table the entry authors must follow, and list statements that would breach 'never decide operator-owned things' (a duplicate receipt class is an operator decision). Deliver {D('scope-keep-cut.tsv')}.""")
add('critic','AttackKillSemantics',f"""Attack the K2 stale-statement mechanism and the correction discipline. Read {C1T} (K2 function), {STALE} and the r28 spot-check ({L}/corpus/lessons/round-28-verifier-spotcheck.md Routed defects 2). K2 accepts any line starting `R29-CORRECTION ` that contains `file:line` after the stale line. Judge: does that force the correction to contain the observed facts? Propose a stricter-only second condition checkable by the tool or by a counting command (e.g. the correction line must contain the literal `152` and `1382` for the r26 statements, or a sha256 pointer), and test in scratch whether an empty-content marker passes today. Also attack the append-only rule: LOG.md and SCORECARD.md line numbers shift if someone inserts text above; what makes K2 robust to line drift (it pins file:line at REV)? Deliver numbered attacks and the strictest feasible fix.""")
add('critic','AttackWavePlan',f"""Attack this wave's own plan. Read {W}/../make-spec.py (read-only; it generates every item) and {PR}. Check: every item names a concrete deliverable or finding; no two items duplicate work (list overlaps, e.g. OpenStatx vs VerifySourcesQuotes vs C3SnapshotPin vs EntryIdentity opening the same pages); dependencies that cannot be satisfied in a single parallel wave (an item that needs another item's delivery); items that give the L1 nothing to integrate; attack share vs the 25% floor; flash-role share vs 50%; whether any claim's kill rule has NO seat attacking it; and whether the seats' write permissions allow their deliverables (paths exist?). Deliver a table item -> verdict (genuine / overlap-with:X / unsatisfiable-dependency / no-integration-value) and the minimum corrections. Do not propose padding.""")
add('critic','AssimilationContractCritic',f"""Check the assimilation plan against the contract in /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/.ufo/prompts/souji-round-29.md lines 440-545 (item 10) clause by clause: source repo read-only (no campaign tool runs); one theme, 1-3 entries; re-ground every cited source in-round with own date and quote; append only rows the admitted entries cite; id collision guard proved on an indented fixture and run; scratch transformation (11 columns, ISO recheck, no pipes, used-by exactly the admitted entries, status mined) with `sources-census.sh validate --file` exit 0 before the first append; quarantine slice hand-check (campaign S118 payload-absent); per-entry gates (PROVINCE scope, QUALITY bar, expansion only on ground not held); Gate records >=1 admit and >=1 reject; considerthese/ absent; doctrine/ not corpus. For each clause state satisfied-by (item or L1 step) or GAP with the minimum fix. Deliver {D('assimilation-clause-table.tsv')}.""")
add('critic','SeparabilityAxes',f"""Attack causal separability and axis attribution (AXES.md: claims are causally separable, on distinct axes, at least one on the lowest axis; Q59 axis-of-surface). Read /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/AXES.md and {PR}. Test: can C1 be measured without C2/C3 landing (its K1 reads rows that C3 appends; its K2 corrects statements about the manifest C2 re-captures — if C2 recaptures r26, the stale statement's subject changes: does the correction still read true after recapture?); can C2 be measured without C1; does C3's coverage move share a surface with C1's registry cell changes (both edit corpus/SOURCES.md — one writer, but are the counters independent)? Is each claim's axis the surface it changes (C1 on `bookkeeping-file` while shipping a tool?). Verify by running each claim's counter on synthetic partial-landing states in scratch. Deliver numbered findings and, where separability fails, the ordering rule (which landing commit must precede which) the L1 must follow.""")
# ---------------- MUTATION TESTERS (6)
add('mutation-tester','MutateC1Forward',f"""Mutation-test the C1 instrument's K1 forward and parsing logic ({C1T}). In a scratch copy under /var/tmp/souji-r29-MutateC1Forward/ create at least 8 mutants (e.g. drop the existence check, replace `\\b` id match with substring, accept 4-space-indented rows, drop the NF==13 check, split used-by only on commas, skip rows after the first blank line, ignore a row id with 4+ digits) and a fixture battery of tiny scratch git repos (per contract) with expected counts. Run the tool and each mutant on the battery; report a kill table (mutant, battery case that kills it, or SURVIVES). For every survivor say whether it is equivalent or a real gap and propose a battery case. Never edit {C1T}.""")
add('mutation-tester','MutateC1ReverseK2',f"""Mutation-test the C1 instrument's K1 reverse and K2 logic ({C1T}). Scratch mutants (>=8): remove the `# ` front-matter stop, treat `- source:` lines as non-source, ignore ids not in rows, drop the `lines[ln:]` after-line restriction (marker before the stale line counts), accept the marker without `file:line`, skip the phrase check, off-by-one on `ln-1`, treat blank stale list as success. Build a battery of scratch git repos (per contract) with expected k1/k2. Report a kill table; survivors named equivalent or real gaps with a battery case each. Never edit {C1T}; the shipped fixture may not exist yet — build your own battery.""")
add('mutation-tester','MutateC2Counter',f"""Mutation-test the frozen C2 counter ({C2C}) in scratch ({S('MutateC2Counter')}). Mutants (>=8): ignore floors, treat mode 120000 blobs as ok records, skip the escape decoder, strip only `./` once vs twice, count the manifest itself as uncovered/not, ignore symlinks.tsv target comparison, compare hash of the blob sha instead of content, return 0 when no manifests exist, take the last duplicate record. Battery: tiny scratch git repos (init with -C) with census/round-N/waves/ trees, each with an expected failed/uncovered/floor result. Report the kill table; survivors named equivalent or real gaps with a battery case. Never edit the counter.""")
add('mutation-tester','MutateCaptureFixtureBase',f"""Mutation-test the BASE capture tool against its existing fixture. Copy {CAP} and {FIX} into scratch ({S('MutateCaptureFixtureBase')}); the fixture only runs in scratch. Create >=8 mutants of the TOOL (e.g. skip manifest self-exclusion, verify disk instead of manifest, drop the special-file refusal, follow symlinks, drop `LC_ALL=C` sort, ignore the nested-dst refusal, skip the source-mismatch comparison, always exit 0) and run the 6-case fixture on each; report which mutants SURVIVE. The survivors define the case set the v2 fixture must kill: list them as required cases, and add the three mutations that model the r28 failure (verify the disk copy, ignore git's ignore rules, drop symlink accounting) and confirm the base fixture does not kill them. Deliver {D('required-fixture-cases.md')}.""")
add('mutation-tester','MutateC3Gates',f"""Mutation-test the C3 gates in scratch ({S('MutateC3Gates')}, clone of the lane at {BASE}). Targets: `tools/souji-gate-check.py` (the entry gate) and `tools/souji-coverage-agreement.py`. Build >=8 entry/row mutants of a stub F3 entry pair: quote absent from snapshot, quote over 25 words, no locator token, snapshot outside --snapshot-dir, missing ADMIT line, missing REJECT line, `source:` id with no row, `ground: F3` entry not named in the README coverage map, map entry path that does not exist, status-column mention only. Run each gate and report which mutant states the gates ACCEPT (false green). Also run `sources-census.sh validate --file` on registry mutants (duplicate id, 12-column row, 10-column row, bad tier, bad status, recheck prose, used-by pointing to a missing path with status mined) and report the census verdict per mutant. Survivors are gaps for the report.""")
add('mutation-tester','MutateGuardAndRows',f"""Mutation-test the assimilation id-collision guard and the row-normalization rules. Scratch ({S('MutateGuardAndRows')}). Using the guard commands in {L}/.ufo/prompts/souji-round-29.md lines 477-484 build registry/staged fixtures: column-zero collision, 1/2/3-space-indented collision, 4-space row (must be ignored), a row with a leading tab, ids S2xx vs S2xxx (4 digits), CRLF line endings, a collision hidden in the Paths section prose. Report which fixtures the guard catches/misses and whether 4-space and tab handling agrees with `scripts/sources-census.sh` (read it, `--file` mode). Then take the four planned rows (campaign ids S117, S118, S122, S136 from {SH}/SOURCES.append.md) and mutate their normalized forms (escaped pipe in anchor, ISO recheck with prose, used-by pointing to an unadopted entry, tier A with kind community) to show each mutant is rejected by `sources-census.sh validate --file`. Report survivors.""")
# ---------------- SENTINELS (2)
add('sentinel','CredScanR26',f"""Credential-shape sentinel for the re-capture. The v2 capture will commit files that were previously kept out of git: the 152 r26 records absent from the committed tree and files under {L}/.ufo/waves/round-26/ that nested .gitignore files hid (the r28 closure attributed 138 to `fixture/` and files under tests/vault/*). BEFORE they are committed, scan the SOURCE tree {L}/.ufo/waves/round-26/, round-27 and round-28 for credential-shaped content: patterns for private key blocks, `op://` refs, bearer/API tokens (sk-, ghp_, xox, AKIA, eyJ JWT shapes), `password=`, `Authorization:`, session cookies. Report only file path, line number, pattern class and a masked excerpt (first 4 characters then `***`); NEVER print a full value. Distinguish fabricated test fixtures (named tests/vault/ fixture files made by earlier rounds' harnesses) from live material. Verdict per path class: safe-to-commit / needs-redaction / route-to-kagi. Never read or touch any file under `~/.config`, `.scratch/` or operator credential stores.""")
add('sentinel','CredScanInputs',f"""Credential and private-URL sentinel for this round's NEW inputs and outputs. Scan (read-only, mask any hit) the staged package inputs this round will read ({SH}/knowledge/corpus/knowledge/duplicate-*.md, near-duplicate-*.md, and the four staged rows in {SH}/SOURCES.append.md), the lane's drafted and delivered files under {W}/ as they appear while you run (re-scan at the end), and the preregistration {PR}. Also scan {L}/census/round-29/ and {L}/tools/souji-registry-agreement.py. Look for op:// references, tokens, session or private URLs (non-public hosts, localhost ports with credentials), home-directory paths of other users, email addresses beyond the lane identity. Report path, line, class, masked excerpt. Verdict clean or the list. Also check whether any seat delivery under {W}/ writes a path outside the permitted directories (read their reports' `## Deliveries`).""")
# ---------------- CONNECTORS (3)
add('connector','CrossClaimOverlap',f"""Cross-claim pattern finder (read-only). Find places where the three claims touch the same bytes or the same assumptions: (1) C2's recapture renames nested `.gitignore` to `.gitignore.captured` and removes/relocates previously committed r26 receipt paths — grep the lane for citations of any `census/round-26/waves/...` path (SCORECARD, LOG, lessons, README, SKILL, QUALITY, tools/souji-landing-gate.py inputs, tests) and tell which would dangle (the lane's pointer gate `python3 -B tools/souji-landing-gate.py` checks backticked paths); (2) C1's K2 pins line numbers in LOG.md/SCORECARD.md/lesson-28 while C3, C1 and the round-end edits append to those files — list which appends can shift a pinned line (appends at the tail cannot; insertions above can) and the landing order that is safe; (3) C3 appends rows to corpus/SOURCES.md while C1 edits used-by cells of other rows in the same table — the single-writer rule and the edit order. Deliver {D('overlap-map.tsv')} and a recommended landing order (C1, C2, C3 or other) with the reason for each dependency.""")
add('connector','CrossSourcePatterns',f"""Cross-source pattern finder (read-only). Compare what the four C3 sources and the lane's existing F3 entry say: statx(2), link(2), cmp(1), Broder 1997, and {L}/corpus/knowledge/dupe-finders-detect-then-act.md (rmlint, jdupes, fdupes, fclones docs/source). Open the man pages yourself. Find: contradictions (e.g. the existing entry's `stat -c '%d:%i'` identity guard vs statx's `stx_dev_*`/`stx_ino` fields; whether a hard-link pair is 'duplicate' under rmlint/fclones defaults vs `cmp`), complementary gaps (what each source adds that the existing entry lacks) and patterns across them (identity before content; three-valued verdicts: same/different/trouble; thresholded vs exact families). Say which statements in the existing entry become better grounded by the new sources (candidates for an append-only link note). Deliver {D('cross-source-patterns.md')} with each pattern citing both sides with <=25-word located quotes.""")
add('connector','CrossLaneAndHistory',f"""Cross-lane and cross-round pattern finder (read-only). (1) Across the lane's own lessons {L}/corpus/lessons/round-2[3-8].md and the six routed defects, find recurring mistake classes (number-drift, reference-drift, attribution) and which QUALITY criteria were meant to catch them (grep Q-numbers); say whether Q60-Q62 (proposed: exclusion-clause reading, committed-bytes receipts, bidirectional used-by) duplicate an existing criterion (Q55 receipts bind rev+sha, Q57 pointer re-derivation, Q58 target derivation) — list the closest existing row for each with a quote. (2) In sibling lanes' corpus/lessons (read-only, /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/*-shokunin/corpus/lessons/round-*.md, grep `used-by`, `manifest`, `committed bytes`, `gitignore`) find any lesson that already solved ignored-evidence capture or bidirectional registry agreement; report lane, file, line. Deliver {D('pattern-map.tsv')} with citations and a recommendation on whether Q60-Q62 are new or should be written as supersessions.""")
