add('revenger','RevengeCaptureFailure',f"""Reverse-engineer the exact causal chain of the r28 C3 failure. Evidence: r28 commits (`git -C {L} log --format='%h %s' -12 {BASE}` and the diff of the capture commit), {CAP}, {L}/census/round-28/records/c3-before.tsv, c3-after.tsv, c3-control.tsv, {L}/.gitignore (and its git history), the r28 wave seat reports under {L}/census/round-28/waves/ (read-only), and the closure text in {L}/corpus/lessons/round-28-verifier-spotcheck.md. Establish: which step created the 152 absent records (which ignore rule file:line at which depth), why the r28 fixture and its verification could not see it (what each check compared), why the 15/14 symlinks are uncovered, what the intent of the original `.gitignore` additions (.ufo/waves/, census/operator-sweep-*/, __pycache__/) was and whether a safe narrower ignore exists, and whether any earlier round (r26/r27) had the same defect in a different surface. Deliver the chain as a numbered list with evidence pointers and the minimal design rule that would have prevented it.""")
add('simplifier','SpecHygiene',f"""Validate this wave's spec hygiene. Read {W}/../make-spec.py (generator) and the rendered plan if present at {W}/../w1-dispatch.json. Check: distinct item ids and distinct prompts; roles only from scout, reviewer, critic, connector, sentinel, executor, mutation-tester, revenger, simplifier, scribe; counts per role equal to executor 21, scribe 10, scout 7, reviewer 8, critic 8, mutation-tester 6, sentinel 2, connector 3, revenger 1, simplifier 2 (total 68); no item asks for a model or routing; every prompt names a surface and a deliverable or finding; every deliverable path sits under {W}/ and no two items write the same path; no item mandates writing outside its scope. Report violations or confirm clean, with the commands you used.""")
add('simplifier','LaneRootStrayCensus',f"""Dry-run hygiene census of the souji lane repo's own top level (the lane practises what it governs; READ-ONLY, propose nothing destructive). List every tracked and untracked top-level entry of {L} (`git -C {L} ls-files | cut -d/ -f1 | sort -u`, `git -C {L} status --porcelain --ignored`) and classify each as live / stale / duplicate / unknown with the evidence (referenced by a gate or fixture? last touched commit?): in particular `err4.nl2`, `err4.z2`, `results/`, `tests/results/`, `tests/fixtures/__pycache__`, `tools/__pycache__`, the many `tools/cand-*`/`impl-*`/`*.impl-*`/`*.r9-s18.sh` candidate files (are they referenced by SKILL.md or any gate? `grep -rl`), `census/round-*/` directories by size (`du -sk`). Per artifact give a receipt status in the lane's taxonomy words (pushed / moved-to-obsidian / stale / none) from `git`, never from guesswork, and a NOT-SAFE default. Deliver {D('lane-stray-census.tsv')} (path, bytes, tracked, referenced-by, last-commit, receipt, proposed-action, reason). Quarantine before delete: you propose; nothing is moved or deleted this round.""")
